Calculate the mean distance between two stars of a galaxy and show that it is much larger than the diameter of a star. Assume that:

(a) the galaxy has spherical symmetry;
(b) the number of stars of the galaxy is $N = 10^{11}$;
(c) the diameter of the galaxy is $D_\mathrm{gal} = 30$ kpc;
(d) the typical diameter of a star inside the galaxy is $D_\mathrm{star} = 1.4 \cdot 10^{11}$ cm.

